Remember, this is just a simple illustration. Real-world brute force attacks can be much more complex and often involve additional techniques like rate limiting, timing attacks, and exploiting specific system vulnerabilities. Additionally, brute force attacks can be detected and mitigated through various security measures, such as account lockouts, CAPTCHAs, and strong password policies.

Always use your programming skills responsibly and ethically.

